// runtime-program-image-fkb-symbol-walk.fk -- Layer 9h6 symbol-addressed PIF micro-walk.
//
// Layer 9h6 is the symbol-level runtime surface for the 9h5 computed
// micro-walker. It consumes a request-ready program-image envelope, an admitted
// 8h6 PIF byte admission, and an 8h8 symbol request. It resolves the request
// internally over the admitted PIF, then walks only the resolved function-root
// entry through 9h5. The receipt carries the computed resolution, micro-walk
// receipt, and trace so agreement is observable.
//
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/source-artifact-cache.fk form-stdlib/source-artifact-descriptor.fk form-stdlib/runtime-artifact-plan.fk form-stdlib/runtime-artifact-selector.fk form-stdlib/runtime-artifact-outcome.fk form-stdlib/runtime-artifact-retry.fk form-stdlib/runtime-artifact-load-envelope.fk form-stdlib/program-image-fkb.fk form-stdlib/program-image-fkb-byte-container.fk form-stdlib/program-image-fkb-byte-file-witness.fk form-stdlib/program-image-fkb-byte-decode.fk form-stdlib/program-image-symbol-entry.fk form-stdlib/runtime-program-image-fkb-walker-trace.fk form-stdlib/runtime-program-image-fkb-micro-walker.fk
